-- Machine Learning
('72000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000031','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000027','supervised-learning','MCQ',1,
'What distinguishes supervised learning from unsupervised learning?',
'[{"id":"a","text":"Supervised learning trains from examples with target labels or values"},{"id":"b","text":"Supervised learning never uses data"},{"id":"c","text":"Unsupervised learning always predicts a labeled target"},{"id":"d","text":"They are identical"}]'::jsonb,
'{"correctOptionId":"a"}'::jsonb,
'{"correctFeedback":"Supervised learning uses labeled targets to learn a predictive relationship.","incorrectFeedback":"Focus on whether the training examples include a target to predict."}'::jsonb,
'["machine-learning","supervised-learning"]'::jsonb,'SEEDED','role-bank-h1',true),
('72000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000032','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000027','data-leakage','MCQ',2,
'Which situation is an example of data leakage?',
'[{"id":"a","text":"A feature contains information that would not be available at prediction time"},{"id":"b","text":"Training on fewer rows than exist in the source table"},{"id":"c","text":"Using a validation set"},{"id":"d","text":"Shuffling training rows"}]'::jsonb,
'{"correctOptionId":"a"}'::jsonb,
'{"correctFeedback":"Leakage occurs when training features expose information unavailable at real prediction time.","incorrectFeedback":"Look for information that improperly crosses the train/prediction-time boundary."}'::jsonb,
'["machine-learning","data-leakage"]'::jsonb,'SEEDED','role-bank-h1',true),
('72000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000027','bias-variance','MCQ',3,
'A model performs poorly on both training and validation data. Which issue is most consistent with that pattern?',
'[{"id":"a","text":"Underfitting / high bias"},{"id":"b","text":"Severe overfitting only"},{"id":"c","text":"Perfect generalization"},{"id":"d","text":"Data leakage is proven"}]'::jsonb,
'{"correctOptionId":"a"}'::jsonb,
'{"correctFeedback":"Poor performance even on training data is a classic sign of underfitting or high bias.","incorrectFeedback":"Overfitting usually has much stronger training performance than validation performance."}'::jsonb,
'["machine-learning","bias-variance","underfitting"]'::jsonb,'SEEDED','role-bank-h1',true),
('72000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000034','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000027','pipeline-leakage','SCENARIO',3,
'You standardize the entire dataset before splitting into train and test sets. What is wrong with this workflow, and how should you fix it?',
null,
'{"referenceAnswer":"Fitting the scaler on all data leaks information from the test set. Split first, fit preprocessing only on the training data, and apply the fitted transformation to validation/test data, ideally inside a pipeline.","expectedKeywords":["leakage","split","training","scaler"]}'::jsonb,
'{"criteria":[{"id":"leakage","weight":0.5,"description":"Identifies test-set information leakage"},{"id":"fix","weight":0.5,"description":"Fits preprocessing on training data only and applies it to held-out data"}],"maxScore":1}'::jsonb,
'["machine-learning","pipeline","data-leakage"]'::jsonb,'SEEDED','role-bank-h1',true),

-- Product Strategy
('72000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000041','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000031','problem-outcome','MCQ',1,
'Which statement is the clearest product outcome rather than an output?',
